Hi [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] 

*I`ve reviewed and I believe a data sharing agreement between 2 separate controllers is definitely required.* Additionally, many of the points in the document re/ data sharing are vaguely defined, and it is not clear what data and how may be shared with the parties.

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
Specific concerns:

* vague wording which makes the description of the transfer unclear, i.e. _“Partner (Bolt) acknowledges that it_ *_can choose_* _to provide Customer Data concerning Applicants”_
* the fact that Bolt will have access to customer Data (which may include Personal Data), including via the Partner Dashboard - not sure this is something that is required for our arrangement, and pursuant to the principle of data minimisation, we want to avoid unnecessary “data transfers”;
* _“To the extent that information is likely to be confidential, at a minimum the Applicant or Customer’s written consent is required”_ - this is unnecessary complication, I agree with your comment in the document.
* no details on how parties will cooperate in case of data breaches, inquiries from authorities, etc. Considering the sensitivity and the extent of the details shared by Bolt, our preference should be to include such procedures - which are outlined in our DSA.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
On a more general note, it is not clear to me why we would have to provide any personal data to the provider, considering that Bolt`s basic function is to distribute the offer from the provider to its merchants.

I would like to clarify the use case with the provider and avoid the data transfer as much as possible if necessary. Bolt`s should not be a part of the “decision making process” regarding the provider`s credit products. 
{panel}

Let's try pushing for our DSA template & share our concerns with the provider. I will prepare a DSA by Thursday & message to clarify the arrangement, as I need to focus on other more priority providers at the moment.

Thanks for the prompt reply [~accountid:5b612cc5e859072d9083d40a] - I can see user_ID and IP in the list, which makes it personal data.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
Additionally, I can see the Card BIN being omitted like this: {{537541XXXXXX7181}}. To understand this correctly - we transferring full BIN with to the provider, but they store the omitted details, correct?
{panel}

Anyways, because the privacy function was able to confirm the personal data transfer is ongoing, I will collaborate with legal to reflect this in the agreement.

