Update the query

*From*

{noformat}(
    sum  (
        increase(nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result{error_code!=\"undefined\"}[1h])
    )  by (node_service_id, system_type, country, provider_method, error_code) 
    - 
    sum (
            increase(nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result{error_code!=\"undefined\"}[1h] offset 7d)
)by (node_service_id, system_type, country, provider_method, error_code)
)
/
sum (
                increase(nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result{error_code!=\"undefined\"}[1h] offset 7d)
) by(node_service_id,system_type,country,provider_method,error_code)*100{noformat}

*To*

{noformat}# 100 * value_now / value_7d_ago - 100 -> percent increase
# for example value_now=80, value_7d_ago=50 -> 100*80/50-100=60 -> 60% increase

(100 * sum  by (node_service_id, status, system_type, country, provider_method, error_code) (
    increase(
        nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result[1h]
    )
)
/
sum  by (node_service_id, status, system_type, country, provider_method, error_code) (
    increase(
        nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result[1h] offset 7d
    )
)) - 100

# filter expression
# we filter out errors based on the error_code and errors count (it needs to be over the threshold)
and
(
    sum  by (node_service_id, status, system_type, country, provider_method, error_code) (
        increase(
            nodejs:payment:payment_status_update_result{
                status="failed",
                error_code!="undefined",
                error_code!="PAYMENT_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS",
            }[1h] offset 7d
        )
    ) > 60  # threshold for error count over the [1h] window
)
{noformat}

The main change is the added threshold of 60, meaning that only errors that were happening more than 1 time per minute 7 days ago are taken into account.

Moreover I have added the kibana query to the alert setting so that we can look at logs for a particular triggering alert instance. Those logs contain payment_attempt_ids in the query.additional_parameter field, so we can also look at cases in admin-panel. Example: [logs|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/UoHRL]

I suggest we monitor how the new configuration does and tune parameters as needed. Right now I have decreased the threshold from 5000 to 100, meaning that only 2x increase in errors will trigger it. This should probably be lowered even more

