CC [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] 

The written email notification is *mandatory* for *Partner account* *consequential suspensions and terminations (couriers and merchants)*. For full transparency, this obligation also only applies in the EU, but for the sake of unity, risk management and also content management (at least from our end) it would be best if we had the same standards everywhere and for all user types, i.e adopt the EU processes everywhere else and include it also for Clients (eaters):

* Outline the paraphrased report and that the report came from 'a third party', e.g “we have received a report stating that”;
* Outline for how long the user is suspended, or if the account has been terminated;
* Reference to T&C’s wording (we are mostly referencing ‘creating an unnecessary safety risk’, for some events such as serving minors/intoxicated users with alcohol we’ve added additional clauses);
* Where to appeal decision (for Partners);
* For fleet couriers, we must also specify which fleet they are in association with, specify the date from which they are suspended/terminated and notify the fleet owner simultaneously.

