Secondly, just to clarify, the link posted “Terms & Conditions (lithuanian) - [https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-delivery-client-pdf/?category=delivery|https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-delivery-client-pdf/?category=delivery]” is an old version of the Client T&Cs and is no longer applicable. The current version is here: [https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-delivery-client/?category=delivery|https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-delivery-client/?category=delivery].

Their comments however are still relevant as the same clauses exist in the latest version. I’ll provide my answers below in {color:#ff5630}red{color}:

* 6.10. Bolt may, at its discretion, provide promotional offers and discounts on the price of the Goods or the Courier Fee. (Terms & Conditions (lithuanian))
There's nothing about it in the first T&C (Terms & Conditions for Partners).
{color:#ff5630}Since this is from the Client T&C it does not create any obligations for the Partner. To the best of my knowledge, such discounts have no effect on the Partner’s operations or the sums they get since Bolt pays the difference in cases where Bolt itself decides to apply a discount. {color}[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] {color:#ff5630}please correct me if I am mistaken here.{color}
