* 10.8. Estonian laws apply to the use of the Bolt Food platform and all legal relationships formed under it. A customer who is a consumer also enjoys the protection of mandatory statutory provisions that would apply in the absence of this clause. (Terms & Conditions (lithuanian))
Shouldn't it be changed in LT tab of T&Cs?
{color:#ff5630}I am not sure what is meant by this comment. Do they mean that the applicable law should be Lithuanian? While we can change the applicable law for the Partner-Bolt relationship (in the Partner Special Terms, if requested by the Partner and approved on our side) then the Partner is not affected by the choice of law for the Client – it is therefore unclear why they should be concerned with this clause at all. {color}
{color:#ff5630}FYI, in the new T&Cs this is in clause 10.9 and slightly re-worded, but the point remains the same.{color}

